    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25534" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διαπίμπλημι</span></b> , aor.
		inf.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-πλῆσαι,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>fill full,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰκίας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.
					<u>Im.</u>
					2.27
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόγων τὴν οἰκουμένην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Eun.
					<u>VS</u>
					p.493D.
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Nonn.
				<u>D.</u>
				5.194
			</span></i>; in early writers in 
				Pass.
			, <i>to be filled with,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					7.85
				</span></i>
			; <i>to be satiated</i> or <i>tired,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διαπεπλησμένος τινός</span>
			<i>of</i> one, <i><span class="en">
				And.
				1.125
			</span></i>.</div>
